scx_qmap: per-PID weight from a pinned BPF map (racing-the-scanner #11)

Adds a BPF_MAP_TYPE_HASH map `pid_weight` (key pid_t tgid, value u32),
pinned by name at /sys/fs/bpf/pid_weight. A task whose PID is in the map gets
its time slice scaled by weight / 100 (100 = the nice-0 default), clamped to
[200us, 1s]; every other task is scheduled exactly as stock scx_qmap.

Base: Linux v7.0 (028ef9c96e96), tools/sched_ext. Apply from the tree root:
  git apply /path/to/scx_qmap_pidweight.patch
  make -C tools/sched_ext scx_qmap
Write weights with scripts/scx_pid_weight.sh; demo: scripts/scx_qmap_demo.sh.

diff --git a/tools/sched_ext/scx_qmap.bpf.c b/tools/sched_ext/scx_qmap.bpf.c
